# Update to FunctionalScript 0.46.0

## Main Changes

- The new Effect system. The main change is that each Effect can have an error, so each Effect returns `Result<T, E>`. The new Effect signature: `Effect<O, T, E>`.
- FunctionalScript now uses `.f.mjs` as the main source file and `types.ts` to describe types. 
  The migration is quite successful, and I would suggest also adapting the idea to use `types.ts` for TypeScript type definitions.

There are also many other changes, and I may have missed something important. 
I would like to see an extensive, structured report on the migration to 0.46.0 once it's done. 
In particular, I'm interested in whether you learned anything new and how you adapted to the project, as well as what the main challenges were.
